As was pointed out, the 60% level is acheived well before reaching
XP=30 with a carefully tuned spellcasting armor kit.

There is an advantage to maxing out XP and spell-tuned armor:
Failure rates for finger of death fall to 0% as you move up and
the damage done by magic missile spell increases as well.  At
some point a combat-wombat Valk can go from using wands
and daggers to using attack-school spells and still be playing
what's essentially a combat-wombat style just with a different
set of "weapons".

To some extent attack spells are like zero-weight auto-charging
wands.  "Z"ap with abandon while your manna lasts, then
switch to wands, then switch to daggers, then take out what
survives all that with two-weaponed artifact-and-saber.

